WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.939
This chart appeared in the 2017

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.709
President's Commission on Combating

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.959
Drug Addiction and the Opioid Crisis

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.609
to demonstrate a link between legal

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.499
opioids like OxyContin and

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.489
overdoses.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.879
One line shows opioid prescriptions

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.059
and another the number of people

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.559
being admitted to treatment centers

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.729
for opioid abuse.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.259
And the third chart two deaths from

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.669
opioid overdoses.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.709
It demonstrates absolutely nothing.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.089
By using a chart like this as

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.829
evidence that the increase in opioid

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.509
prescriptions caused the overdose

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.919
crisis. Government officials

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.209
committed the most rudimentary

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.859
statistical error of all, which is

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.449
to assume that correlation proves

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.379
causation.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.179
Global avocado production also

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.469
climbed in these years.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.059
My age also went up.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.619
Does that mean avocado production in

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.089
my age might have something to do

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.319
with the increase in overdose

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.309
deaths?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.379
No. While it's at least plausible

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.519
that an increase in opioid

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.169
prescriptions led to an increase in

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.179
overdoses, you can't determine

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.739
that simply by noting parallel

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.119
increases. The purpose of

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.069
statistical analysis is to test

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.959
our theories and assumptions, and

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.849
this chart fails miserably in

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.899
that regard.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.009
The way it's drawn in the

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.109
Commission's published report also

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.579
gives the misimpression that the

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.139
rates of increase for these three

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.789
lines were about the same.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.199
Actually, all three lines are

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.789
measured in different units and the

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.649
chart should look more like this.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.999
Another red flag.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.399
This chart doesn't go past 2010,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.689
even though the report came out in

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.159
2017.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.389
There's a reason for that.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.619
In the years that followed, the

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.269
pattern rapidly reversed, with

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.769
opioid prescriptions falling

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.389
dramatically while drug related

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.339
deaths continued to increase.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.929
The use of charts like this one,

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.219
which is part of the government's

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.139
failure to correctly understand

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.879
and respond to the opioid overdose

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.709
crisis, has caused enormous human

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.419
suffering. The government has pushed

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.399
doctors to severely limit opioid

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.079
prescriptions for pain patients

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.879
through laws, regulations and the

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.049
threat of civil and criminal

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:46.979
penalties.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.109
And today, thousands of Americans

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.609
with chronic and debilitating

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.469
illnesses are unable to access

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.849
drugs that could alleviate their

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.859
pain. This chart from the CDC

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.049
gives us a clear picture of events.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.699
Drug related deaths involving

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.439
commonly prescribed opioids like

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.049
hydrocodone and oxycodone,

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.819
did rise in the first decade of the

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.709
21st century, but then

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.538
leveled off for the first

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:11.519
ten years. The increase in overdoses

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.259
correlated with increases in the

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.059
prescriptions for those

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.609
prescriptions filled after 2010

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.589
with no reduction in overdoses.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.479
What we did see in 2010 was

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.489
an increase in illegal heroin use

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.319
and in 2013

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.299
and even sharper rise in overdoses

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.859
from fentanyl and other synthetic

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.659
opioids rarely used in legal

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.559
medicine.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.329
This was likely caused by a change

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.859
in the business practices of drug

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.809
cartels and the fact that fentanyl

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.609
is cheaper and easier to smuggle

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.539
than heroin.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.369
During this period, fentanyl, which

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.229
is more potent than heroin,

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.849
became increasingly common as a

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.799
heroin booster and substitute.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.659
If heroin were legal, most

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.309
of these overdose deaths probably

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.779
would not have occurred.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.009
The governments clamp down on

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.019
prescription opioids also probably

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.299
exacerbated the overdose crisis.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.489
The blockbuster pain drug OxyContin

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.679
became available in 1996.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.689
Three years later, we do indeed see

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.069
a rise in deaths involving

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.329
prescription opioids.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.919
But that does not necessarily mean

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.419
those deaths involve people who

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.219
obtain prescriptions from doctors.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.709
National survey data from 2013

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.749
and 2014 indicated

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.129
that most people who misused

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.019
prescription pain relievers reported

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.039
getting them from a friend or

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.059
relative.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.559
Then a quarter said they obtain the

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.909
drugs from doctors.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.859
A survey of OxyContin addicted

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:28.279
people entering rehab from 2001

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.239
to 2004 found

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.219
that 78% had never been

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.109
prescribed the medication, and among

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.179
the 22% who had been prescribed

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.429
OxyContin, nearly all had substance

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.959
abuse problems before taking the

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.799
drug.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.719
So if they weren't taking OxyContin,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.739
they would likely would have been

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.059
taking something else.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.889
The stereotype of a clean living

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.659
person getting hooked on opioids,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.759
originally prescribed for pain

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.169
and then suffering a fatal or

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.359
non-fatal overdose is not common

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.319
in the data.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.849
As prescription opioids became

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.569
harder to find in the black market,

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.359
many non-medical users of these

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.489
drugs likely turned to heroin

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.619
contaminated with fentanyl, putting

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.759
them at a much higher risk of

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.629
overdosing.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.739
They were replaced illegally,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.389
produced, reliably dosed

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.279
pharmaceuticals with black market

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.989
drugs whose potency is highly

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.609
variable and unpredictable.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.588
If we widen the time span, we see

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.239
that overall drug overdose deaths

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.559
have been increasing at a fairly

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.838
steady rate since 1979

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:23.879
or 17 years before OxyContin

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.919
became available and continuing long

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.509
after illegal use of opioids was

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.829
severely cut back.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.239
During the same period, we see

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.919
parallel increases in deaths from

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.749
suicide and alcohol abuse

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.819
or so-called deaths of despair.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:36.809
There have also been steady

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.249
increases in diagnoses of

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.389
depression.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.159
This suggests that many deaths ruled

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.749
accidental overdoses could be

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.789
deliberate suicides, or perhaps

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.049
they were partially deliberate.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.489
Although this is correlation, not

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.019
causation. So we don't know for

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.849
sure. The data also suggests that

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.679
the underlying cause of the overdose

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.389
crisis is more fundamental than

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.099
overprescribing of opioids.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.019
Back around 2010, when

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.399
opioid prescriptions were still

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.339
rising. Alongside overdoses.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.959
It was plausible to investigate a

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.459
link, but none of them took the

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.079
correct approach, which would be to

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.939
compare similar patients, one of

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.679
whom got a prescription for opioids

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.029
and the other who did not.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.709
Such match pairs shouldn't just be

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.479
checked for overdose deaths, which,

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.269
after all, affect only 0.04%

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.249
of patients, but for overall health

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.539
and quality of life.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.219
Instead, researchers compared

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.259
unmatched samples of patients, some

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.819
of whom received higher doses of

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.959
opioids in others.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.819
One influential and heavily cited

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.949
study published in 2011

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.179
in the Journal of the American

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.009
Medical Association, began with

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.049
a sample of 750 veterans

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.729
health patients who received opioid

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.559
prescriptions for pain and later

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.389
died of opioid overdoses.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.099
It compared them to a random sample

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.959
of 155,000 other

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.699
veterans health patients who also

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.379
received opioid prescriptions and

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.909
didn't die of overdoses.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.799
It found that the high dose opioid

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.359
prescriptions were more likely to

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.249
lead to fatalities, a finding that

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.929
was used to support the CDC

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.789
guidelines for strongly discouraging

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.749
large doses.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.429
The problem with this study is that

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.319
the high dose and low dose patients

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.729
differed in many ways.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.319
In particular, the high dose

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.149
patients presumably had more severe

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.589
pain and more serious medical

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.329
issues. They may have also differed

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.919
in the type of pain they endured or

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.479
the length of time they suffered.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.069
Controls have to match subjects as

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.389
closely as possible.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.099
This study did not meet that basic

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.839
requirement of good science.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.969
It is plausible that in the 750

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.829
patients who overdosed did so for

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.239
reasons other than the amount of

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.009
opioids they were prescribed for

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:29.329
reasons the study couldn't control

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.489
for, 40% have been diagnosed

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.259
with substance abuse disorders in

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.759
the 12 months before getting an

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.159
opioid prescription, 66%

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.209
had been diagnosed with a

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.649
psychiatric disorder.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:40.699
A population with these

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.529
characteristics is likely to have a

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:43.939
higher than normal frequency of

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.919
overdose death with or without legal

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.389
opioid prescriptions.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.189
Perhaps most important, the study

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.079
ignores the benefits of opioid pain

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.119
relief to 155,000

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.799
patients who didn't overdose.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.689
Even if taking prescription opioids

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.369
does increase the risk of overdose

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.989
deaths, but the study doesn't

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:01.609
demonstrate. Many patients would

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.049
gladly accept the risk for the

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:04.549
quality of life improvement of

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.689
diminished pain.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.999
An influential 2010 study

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.529
published in the Annals of Internal

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.569
Medicine also attempted to show

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.249
that higher prescribed doses of

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.929
opioids correlated with a higher

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.549
risk of death from overdose.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.899
But within the study group, there

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.519
were just six patients who died of

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.439
opioid overdoses, fewer

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.329
than the number of study authors.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.979
Yet the authors claim statistically

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.899
significant results after adjusting

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:28.819
for smoking, depression, substance

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.769
abuse, comorbid conditions, pain,

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.809
side age, sex, recent sedative,

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.489
hypnotic prescription, and recent

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.319
initiation of opioid use.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.369
This is absurd.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.139
It would take at least 100 patients

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.339
who died to estimate the

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.989
adjustments, much less make any

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:43.219
conclusions with statistical

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:44.029
confidence.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.619
The authors even conceded that it

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.209
was not established whether their

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:48.589
results were due to patient

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.149
differences or direct effect of

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.109
higher dose.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.219
In other words, the study

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.779
demonstrates nothing. Although they

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.189
are more than a decade old, these

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:56.809
studies continue to be cited by

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:57.949
public health officials and

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.679
policymakers, including the 2017

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.359
President's Commission on Combating

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:03.709
Drug Addiction and the Opioid

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.179
crisis, which relied almost

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:06.649
completely on studies published

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:08.809
before 2014, which generally

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:11.389
used data collected before 2011.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.909
Again, there's no mystery as to why,

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.159
only by relying on outdated studies

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.079
could the prescription opioids cause

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.239
the crisis narrative be sustained.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.439
Government officials haven't

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.119
reckoned with the abysmal failure of

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.499
limiting access to prescription

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.819
opioids.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.049
Rather, they've doubled down on the

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.909
policy while citing and promoting

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:30.829
statistically flawed studies based

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.779
on stale data and promoting

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.519
charts that conspicuously cut off

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.168
before the data start to undermine

00:08:36.169 --> 00:08:37.489
their chosen policy.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.048
No one has yet demonstrated that

00:08:39.049 --> 00:08:40.969
patients prescribed opioids are more

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.798
likely to suffer overdoses than

00:08:42.799 --> 00:08:44.359
match patients who were denied them.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.589
No one has shown that overall

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.599
quality of life and life expectancy

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.429
are lower for opioid patients.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.929
The first step to arriving at a

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.669
serious policy response to the

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.679
overdose crisis is to take an honest

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.089
look at the problem by using

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.649
statistical techniques to gain a

00:08:57.650 --> 00:08:59.089
deeper understanding of its root

00:08:59.090 --> 00:08:59.989
causes.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.729
